review_text:
the big update is finally here and oh boy, does it deliver
i've put in about 20 hours in as of writing and i can definitely say that my experience was way more positive than negative
i'm gonna go more into complaints just because it feels important to address but overall they're not really too big of a deal
i'm not gonna bring up bugs because it'd be stupid to because they'd be fixed
though i will say at first i didn't really like playing it but it definitely grew on me a lot after playing for a while

- THE GOOD
)weapons feel better than ever and have wonderful sound design

)movement is great, feels really responsive

)the visuals are fantastic

)banger ost

)just generally fun to play

- THE BAD
)early game
the early game definitely needs to be improved somehow because even though i was able to get through it, i can see it being hard to get into (and it was for me at first)
getting new weapons or equipment to use can be pretty annoying because of key rng so a lot of the time you just end up using the starter pistol, and shards are initially very slow to get
cards are cool but are either too strong or restrict early game variety if you don't have them (though it's mostly because it can be pretty difficult to obtain weapons and equipment without them)

)variety 
while a pretty major issue is expected since the game is early in development, so it'll just improve over time
however tablets lack a lot of options and don't really have perks that interact with your weapons and really is the biggest thing with variety bothering me

)meta progression 
this isn't a thing that bothers me in games but the implementation is not that great here
mostly just because it takes EXTREMELY long to unlock everything, i've only gotten about half of the upgrades.
just to get any meaningful amount of jade vines you basically require the fool perk, and even then that's barely anything
the underdark is also like the only way to farm jade vines quickly, and i have a lot of problems with it
(also add a reload speed upgrade please :,)

)threat level/enemies
threat level is key to the game but like the rate that it increases is so ridiculous that i'm just kinda numb to it
it scales way too fast and enemies just appear in such ridiculously high numbers that it feels overwhelming a lot of the time
it doesn't feel very meaningful and creates a lot of artificial difficulty by scaling enemy count, hp and damage

)the underdark
neat idea but just an absolute clusterfuck, needs major changes to actually be fun
enemies are everywhere and have like 2x the health of regular stages so a lot of weapons are just terrible to use
there is a massive lack of variety in rooms and a lot of the rooms are extremely claustrophobic

)keys/bunkers
i don't have actually any major issues with these it's just that keys are super random to get
and i also wish that there were other ways to get weapons/tablets so it weren't so reliant on bunkers

)equipment
mostly just really underpowered and scales really badly, at some point i just stopped using them altogether
(stim is good tho)

)minor stuff
the workbench is practically worthless because of build a gun, but the workbench is just their for future features so i can kind of forgive it
build a gun is super cool but for later in development should definitely be harder to get to feel more rewarding

ALSO just before what i'd like to see, the game needs to better explain mechanics, there's a lot of things that i used in my runs that i still have no idea what they do (static damage (which also might just not be working)), and also i played for like 10 hours thinking i couldn't use the ultimate until later :)
and the scanner feature that just isn't mentioned anywhere i think
(an in game wiki/archive would be pretty cool telling you just what weapons, their upgrades, enemies and tablet perks do as you unlock them)

- FUTURE WISHES
)more variety (duh, but definitely embrace the rogue-like nature and add a bunch of tablet stuff)

)better workbench functionality and importance

)threat level rework

)underdark rework (i saw somebody in the reviews mention how you could have multiple doors showing what's in that room or the rewards for it like in hades that would be pretty rad i think)

)ways to get items without having to use bunkers (weapon crates / tablets just appearing in the level sometimes)

)build a gun should scale price based on weapon strength (not really necessary i just think some of them are stupid strong)

anyway i think this is a very good direction for the game and a great base for the future
i don't know if this'll be seen but i'm really hopeful for the game and excited to see what's next
(and i would love to see the level editor return at some point in the future because that was fun as hell)
